# Commit these changes → go live

When the user says **"commit these changes"** (or similar: "commit and deploy", "ship it", "push live"), run the full deploy pipeline in one turn.

## Pipeline (always in this order)

1. `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` — draft an accurate commit message.
2. Stage and commit relevant files.
3. Push immediately after a successful commit:
   ```bash
   git push origin HEAD
   ```
4. Verify with `git status` — branch must not be "ahead of origin".
5. Confirm to the user: **changes are pushed and Vercel will deploy live** (typically ~1 min).

## Trigger phrases

- "commit these changes" ← primary
- "commit and deploy" / "ship it" / "push live" / "go live"

## Do NOT push when

- User says "commit but don't push" or "local commit only"
- Commit failed or pre-commit hook rejected it
- Nothing to commit

## If push fails

- Show the error; never ask for tokens in chat.
- User can re-auth once in terminal: `git push origin HEAD`
